From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Preserve presentation owner between swapchains

THE FINALS repeatedly destroys and recreates its Vulkan swapchain on the
same VkSurface. When its last swapchain is destroyed, deactivate excludes
the current client from both owner searches. With no other client this
clears the owner and detaches the subsurface. Detaching replaces the opaque
carrier with a transparent SHM buffer, exposing the desktop until the next
swapchain attaches the same client again.

Use the existing update_owner policy on deactivation: prefer the newest
active client, otherwise retain the current registered owner. A zero active
count between swapchains does not mean that the graphics surface or window
has been destroyed. Keeping the subsurface also avoids invalidating its
attachment and presentation generations during an ordinary swapchain gap.

Actual client destruction/detachment still unregisters the surface and
selects a replacement. Visibility and role changes still detach clients
through the existing attach checks. Active replacement presenters retain
priority; inactive probe surfaces cannot displace a displayed frame merely
because its swapchain is being recreated.

The new #754 log contains 129 activations of the same 0x100c2 client, with
128 intervening deactivate/recreate cycles and no client-size warnings.
This fixes the unnecessary detach during those cycles, without suppressing
WSI out-of-date results or changing the working overlay focus fix.

This corrects GE's activation/deactivation extension of the native-presenter
coordination originally implemented by Erhan Bilgili (nanomatters).
Link: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/754#issuecomment-5594967486
---
diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -4919,18 +4919,12 @@ static BOOL wayland_client_surface_is_candidate(struct client_surface *client)
 static void wayland_client_surface_deactivate(struct client_surface *client)
 {
-    struct wayland_client_surface *surface = impl_from_client_surface(client);
-    struct wayland_client_surface *owner;
     struct wayland_win_data *data;
 
     if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(client->hwnd))) return;
 
-    if (!ReadAcquire(&client->active_ref) && data->client_surface == surface)
-    {
-        owner = wayland_client_surface_find_owner(data, surface, TRUE);
-        if (!owner) owner = wayland_client_surface_find_owner(data, surface, FALSE);
-        wayland_client_surface_set_owner(data, owner);
-    }
-    wayland_client_surfaces_attach(data, NtUserGetAncestor(client->hwnd, GA_ROOT));
+    /* Keep the last frame attached across swapchain recreation. Only another
+     * active presenter, or actual surface detachment/destruction, replaces it. */
+    wayland_client_surface_update_owner(data);
     TRACE("deactivated %s\n", debugstr_client_surface(client));
     wayland_win_data_release(data);
 }
